cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use estheRineq in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "estheRineq: Epidemiological Statistics Toolkit for Health Inequality Estimation and Reporting in R"
abstract: >-
  R toolkit uniting complex-survey health econometrics (rank-dependent concentration
  indices, exact influence-function variance, need standardization, horizontal inequity,
  Wagstaff and RIF-Oaxaca decompositions) and epidemiological surveillance and reporting
  (all 21 WHO Health Inequality Monitor measures, logistic and Poisson SII/RII, Pelotas
  equiplots, standardized mortality/morbidity rates, and STROBE-Equity 2025 reporting).
authors:
